sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User (Web / Mobile, not signed in)
    participant GW as Kong :8080
    participant ID as ms-identity :8081
    participant RC as RecoveryCodePort (in-memory)
    participant NOT as ms-notification :8088
    participant SMTP as SMTP relay

    Note over GW: All three routes below are public bootstrap routes (see SEQ-02) — the edge pre-function does not require a bearer for them

    rect rgb(238, 245, 238)
    Note over U,RC: 1. Request a code — POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password {email}
    U->>GW: POST /api/v1/auth/forgot-password {email}
    GW->>ID: forward (public route)
    ID->>ID: load user by email
    alt unknown or inactive user
        Note right of ID: anti-enumeration — no code is issued, nothing is logged beyond a generic line
    else within the 60s resend cooldown for this email
        ID->>RC: issue(email, ttl=10min)
        RC-->>ID: null (throttled)
        Note right of ID: a code is already live — no new one is generated or sent
    else eligible
        ID->>RC: issue(email, ttl=10min)
        RC-->>ID: {code (6 digits), ttl}
        ID->>ID: hash code SHA-256, store in memory (10 min TTL, 5 attempts, 60s resend cooldown)
        ID->>NOT: POST /api/v1/emails {to, template: "verification_code", data: {code, minutes}} — internal network only, no Kong route
        alt SMTP_HOST configured
            NOT->>SMTP: send verification_code e-mail
            SMTP-->>NOT: accepted
            NOT-->>ID: 200
        else SMTP_HOST empty
            NOT-->>ID: 202 {status: "skipped"}
            Note right of NOT: no e-mail actually leaves the system — the code still lives in identity's memory either way
        end
        opt notification unreachable or errors
            ID->>ID: log a warning only — the code stays valid, a resend after the cooldown will try again
        end
    end
    ID-->>U: 202 {status: "accepted"} — always, regardless of which branch above ran
    end

    rect rgb(240, 245, 255)
    Note over U,RC: 2. Verify the code — POST /api/v1/auth/verify-code {email, code}
    U->>GW: POST /api/v1/auth/verify-code {email, code}
    GW->>ID: forward (public route)
    ID->>ID: validate code is exactly 6 digits
    ID->>RC: verify(email, code) — constant-time compare against the SHA-256 hash
    alt code matches, not expired, attempts remaining
        RC-->>ID: true — challenge marked verified
        ID-->>U: 200 {status: "verified"}
    else wrong code, expired, or 5 attempts already used
        RC-->>ID: false
        ID-->>U: 401 "Invalid or expired code" (one message for all three cases — no detail on which)
    end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 246, 236)
    Note over U,RC: 3. Reset the password — POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password {email, password}
    U->>GW: POST /api/v1/auth/reset-password {email, password}
    GW->>ID: forward (public route)
    ID->>ID: validate the new password against the active password_policy (checked BEFORE consuming the challenge, so a bad password does not burn the verified code)
    alt password fails the policy
        ID-->>U: 400 validation error — the verified challenge is untouched, the user can retry reset directly
    else password valid
        ID->>RC: consumeVerified(email) — single use
        alt no verified challenge for this email
            RC-->>ID: false
            ID-->>U: 401 "Verification code required" (same message whether the account is unknown or just never verified — no enumeration)
        else verified challenge present
            RC-->>ID: true
            ID->>ID: BCrypt-hash the new password, update app_user.password_hash
            ID->>ID: load every user_session for this user and close the Active ones
            ID->>ID: publish identity-events {type: "PasswordChanged", userId} — best-effort, no consumer exists (see communication-patterns.md §2)
            ID-->>U: 200 {status: "updated"}
        end
    end
    end

    Note over U,ID: Mobile never calls POST /api/v1/auth/refresh after this — a fresh login is required, same as after any other session close (see SEQ-02 §4)
